{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate","id":1226163,"title":"Obfuscate ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-09T19:48:16-07:00","id":1226163,"title":"Obfuscate ?","content":"I am struggling with the Cloak of Night dot of obfuscate. My player keeps trying various things and I just don\u2019t know if it\u2019s within the scope of the power. <br /> <br /> 1. Can he carry someone, making himself invisible to make her look like she is floating? Who notices?<br /> <br /> 2 can he just reach into someone\u2019s pocket unnoticed? <br /> <br /> 3 can he open doors and slam doors ( acting like a ghost to scare people) all while staying unnoticed? <br /> <br /> (I know there were more but I can\u2019t recall now. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  Meant cloak of Night 06-09-2018, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T19:59:06-07:00","id":1226167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate#post1226163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am struggling with the touch of shadow dot of obfuscate. My player keeps trying various things and I just don\u2019t know if it\u2019s within the scope of the power.<br /> <br /> 1. Can he carry someone, making himself invisible to make her look like she is floating? Who notices?<br /> <br /> 2 can he just reach into someone\u2019s pocket unnoticed?<br /> <br /> 3 can he open doors and slam doors ( acting like a ghost to scare people) all while staying unnoticed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch of Shadow is an extension of Face in the Crowd, allowing you to use it on objects and animals. It makes your perception slide off them, but it doesn't make them invisible. You would see someone holding that person, but you wouldn't focus on them because they're not really attention grabbing.<br /> <br /> Reaching into someone's pocket would probably count as gathering that person's attention, just like opening doors and slamming them would. It would likely institute the roll to gain notice of the vampire.<br /> <br /> Now, it's possible you're talking about Cloak of Night, which is more of a straight invisibility power. A vampire using it could use it to carry someone and make it look like they're floating (they would have to be posing properly, I think if you're carrying someone normally they're going to look like they're being carried, so you would have a sort of 'bad CGI' situation where it's clear someone is there you just can't see them). You can reach into people's pockets unnoticed or open and slam doors, though these likely count as the 'indirect clues' that can be used to track them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T20:01:25-07:00","id":1226169,"title":"","content":"Cloak of night! You\u2019re right! Third dot is what I meant indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T20:04:10-07:00","id":1226171,"title":"","content":"How do I narratively justify player carrying around a girl on his shoulders in a bar and have no one see him when they can see her? <br /> <br /> Wouldn\u2019t the person\u2019s pocket being picked feel being touched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T20:36:11-07:00","id":1226178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226171#post1226171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I narratively justify player carrying around a girl on his shoulders in a bar and have no one see him when they can see her?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is the player narratively justifying this being done in the first place without also using the power's free effect to make her ignored?<br /> <br /> Follow up on the fact that this is a modification of Face in the Crowd \u2014 they're drawing attention and therefore everybody around is going to be rolling Wits + Composure - Obfuscate to notice that something weird is going on.<br /> <br /> Remember: Obfuscate isn't an invisibility power in the sense of bending light and photons, it's an invisibility power in the sense that you are <i>compelling people to disregard your presence</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn\u2019t the person\u2019s pocket being picked feel being touched? </div> </div> </div>Cloak of Night's basic invisibility is more properly stated as &quot;the vampire does not directly register in the perception of other people&quot; \u2014 you could bump shoulders with two dozen people crossing a crowded room and they'd be none the wiser, because &quot;there's something touching me&quot; gets elided over in people's minds just like &quot;the sheriff is wearing very jangly spurs&quot; does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T20:51:50-07:00","id":1226186,"title":"","content":"I did say it was part of face in the crowd and carrying someone while invisible is specifically drawing attention.<br /> <br /> When someone visible is involved and say she is using awe to draw attention to herself, wouldn\u2019t everyone notice she is floating in the air then ask themselves, how is she up there. Thus notice him holding her?<br /> <br /> So if you had the third dot of obfuscate it would be like sleight of hand merit where you can just take anything you want when you want it without having to roll? Could you then just walk into a bank, swipe the keys, empty the vault and walk right out?<br /> <br /> I meant more specifically if Player and victim were the only people in the room at the time. A crowded bar, it's almost expected that someone will bump into you, but if you are alone in your office where no one else is suppose to be. ... It's harder to brush off that... someone just touched me feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-10-2018, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T21:17:05-07:00","id":1226190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226186#post1226186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you had the third dot of obfuscate it would be like sleight of hand merit where you can just take anything you want when you want it without having to roll? Could you then just walk into a bank, swipe the keys, empty the vault and walk right out?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually why most banks close before sundown.<br /> <br /> Then vampires sent ghouls, but banks started depositing into the federal reserve so they don't have as much cash on hand as media suggests.<br /> <br /> Supernaturals are powerful, and their abilities are not balanced against the mortal world. They do have the tradition of the masquerade, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T21:17:09-07:00","id":1226191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226186#post1226186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone visible is involved and say she is using awe to draw attention to herself, wouldn\u2019t everyone notice she is floating in the air then ask themselves, how is she up there? Thus notice him holding her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Obfuscate and Majesty have &quot;never mind that&quot; as part and parcel of their baseline effect \u2014 &quot;all eyes fall on the vampire <i>and nobody cares what he's doing</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, what is this hypothetical even for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you had the third dot of obfuscate it would be like sleight of hand merit where you can just take anything you want when you want it without having to roll? </div> </div> </div>The things in a mark's pockets are not themselves Obfuscated and being accomplished at Obfuscate doesn't directly translate to transcendent skill at Larceny. You'd add your Obfuscate dots to your roll or subtract it from their roll to notice they were being pickpocketed, but &quot;I cannot put my senses on the direct presence of Phantasmo the Vampire&quot; doesn't translate to &quot;I can't put two and two together when my phone isn't in my pocket thirty seconds after I placed a call.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you then just walk into a bank, swipe the keys, empty the vault and walk right out? </div> </div> </div>What part of opening the vault are you supposing is a facet of the vampire's direct presence?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T21:57:05-07:00","id":1226199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226191#post1226191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of opening the vault are you supposing is a facet of the vampire's direct presence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry. I do not understand your question. <br /> <br /> <br /> I get that there is that \u201cnobody cares factor\u201d but there is also a \u201cthat\u2019s impossible\u201d factor. People can\u2019t just float around singing and dancing in a crowded bar. So would that give them at least a roll to notice or would they automatically notice the vampire holding her up on his shoulder? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2014-<br /> To clarify: So opening and closing doors in an office where it\u2019s just vampire and victim leads to They would potentially notice the vampire with a roll. <br /> ( or even in a crowded bar? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T22:06:10-07:00","id":1226200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226199#post1226199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that there is that \u201cnobody cares factor\u201d but there is also a \u201cthat\u2019s impossible\u201d factor. People can\u2019t just float around singing and dancing in a crowded bar. So would that give them at least a roll to notice or would they automatically notice the vampire holding her up on his shoulder?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no disbelief, and mortals don't have a power that activates a Clash of Wills like that. Another vampire could probably figure it out and use Auspex, but for a mortal it looks like she's floating oddly and thinking that that's impossible doesn't change it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To clarify: So opening and closing doors in an office where it\u2019s just vampire and victim leads to They would potentially notice the vampire with a roll.<br /> ( or even in a crowded bar? ) </div> </div> </div>It says this in the Discipline description for Face in the Crowd, 'If he\u2019s doing something that would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent, everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice the commotion, penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots.' Keep in mind, they are not invisible, they're just unobtrusive. There is someone standing there but it's such a bland someone your attention doesn't let you focus on them. You have to roll just to even notice them doing something like slamming doors.<br /> <br /> For Cloak of Night, they're effectively invisible, if Alucard picks up Julie in the middle of a rooftop party and throws her over the side of the building, Julie's the only one who saw the vampire do it. Barring some other supernatural involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2018, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T22:33:38-07:00","id":1226203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226199#post1226199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry. I do not understand your question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cloak of Night stops people from noticing that there's a person where you are. It does not make them fail to notice that a bank vault is open or anything else that is not a direct part of &quot;there's something here, yes, here, standing six feet in front of me holding my keys.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that there is that \u201cnobody cares factor\u201d but there is also a \u201cthat\u2019s impossible\u201d factor. </div> </div> </div>You narrowed this hypothetical to <i>specifically </i> &quot;what if the character who isn't benefiting from psychic invisibility is using the power that draws everyone's attention to them?&quot; and that power means they don't care if the character in question is stark naked, covered in blood, and waving a poleaxe around the dance floor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So would that give them at least a roll to notice or would they automatically notice the vampire holding her up on his shoulder? </div> </div> </div>They're getting a roll to notice and they can pin down the vampire's position from context clues per the extended action notes.<br /> <br /> This is <i>still </i>coming across as a very bizarre and nonsensical hypothetical to fixate upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T23:16:39-07:00","id":1226210,"title":"","content":"I am fixated because I felt like I was not really getting a straight answer. Though nofather cleared some things up. <br /> <br /> And ... made a new question. So what would the people at the rooftop party see? Julie floating, struggling and screaming to the edge, then suddenly falling over? <br /> <br /> And it wasn\u2019t a hypothetical... it happened in game and I wanted to know if I handled it properly or not. So you can think it was as nonsensical as you want. People think of strange things in games and even experienced people get thrown for loops...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T23:31:55-07:00","id":1226211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226210#post1226210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And ... made a new question. So what would the people at the rooftop party see? Julie floating, struggling and screaming to the edge, then suddenly falling over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, like she was having a fit of some sort or was just swept across the area. Some witnesses would probably suffer Breaking Points, some might think she went and jumped on her own, others that she was picked up by something supernatural but they really don't want to dwell on it.<br /> <br /> It's the kind of thing protectors of the masquerade and hunters look out for. Especially since it's so easy to do it subtly, if the vampire just used Cloak of Night on the human no one would have noticed her doing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T06:55:20-07:00","id":1226236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226163-obfuscate?p=1226210#post1226210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you can think it was as nonsensical as you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let me be clearer: You said your player keeps trying various things and then completely neglected to give any further context for the strangest action in question \u2014 you didn't mention Awe until after I pointed out that Obfuscate compels ignorance and then you immediately jumped to two examples framed as hypotheticals that bent the scenario in ways it presumably did not also play out.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate is a power for going unseen, filtered through the core ability of the vampire to be specifically and personally unremarkable as long as they don't act in remarkable ways. The ability to vanish completely from outside perception adds a price in the stuff that a vampire needs to be not-dead, as does the ability to extend their regular ignorability to other subjects. It is going to default to outcomes that do not make the vampire using Obfuscate stand out, but this does not translate to people treating an activity that usually hinders someone's use of their arms as though it were stage-magic levitation.<br /> <br /> &quot;My player and another vampire tried invoking a goofy perceptual-steering paradox in mortal space despite this costing Vitae and being the sort of thing vampire society frowns upon&quot; is the sort of thing one usually expects a <i>why</i> for, particularly if your main problem is how it presents itself rather than that they keep doing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T11:22:33-07:00","id":1226266,"title":"","content":"I can appreciating wanting to know more about the situation, but I've found the more you ask the more deviation the answer allows for, and often the hypothetical turns into something an ST character did. And criticizing the situation doesn't help, even if it hasn't happened yet. People really don't want to be told how to run the game at their table, even if they seem to ask for it.<br /> <br /> Unless the player said their vampire lifted the girl over his head, her fighting the entire way (because it's an attack and she can see her attacker through Cloak of Night) I'd have it appear more like a 'dragged by some invisible force to the edge.' But either way it's the kind of thing that causes attention in the way vampires specifically don't want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}